  "2026-10-25T21:45:21.508Z",codex-agent,"Repair commit a735bd1 passed full CI: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40236418608 . All 4 jobs (Node 22, Node 26, npm release gate, Bun release gate) succeeded. Every job ran 423/423 tests in both V8 and independent statement passes, zero failures/skips. All 9 required sources: 1580/1580 statements and 100% lines/branches/functions. CodeQL also passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40236418649 . This is the requested full-gate evidence; duplicate local release runs were interrupted after CI completed and are not counted as successful local full gates. Completed local full V8 pass was 423/423 at 100% lines/branches/functions; latest linked targeted command 6/6, restored revert cases 11/11, typecheck and 92 documented declarations passed. No standalone lint script exists."
  "2026-10-25T21:45:23.842Z",codex-agent,"Final review matrix: 82 observed boundaries, 164 fault cells (82 actual local edits and 82 real worker SIGKILL interruptions) across terminal import, fresh export, relation export, pending-export recovery and mixed sync. All passed in both CI coverage passes. Both reported races are fixed. Repeated mapped edits after PATCH also converge using ordered historical operation proofs; independent exporter processes allocate one remote identity. Remaining acceptance limit is the documented ambiguous-create dispatch state: no second POST is issued, but an actually unsent request cannot automatically converge without an additional provider uniqueness/recovery contract. No approval to resend has been assumed. SDK terminal-match API gap remains on pm-ado-sdk-match-close-1025 for orchestrator reporting. Releasing adoption claim for verification; neither item is closed."
  "2026-10-26T03:25:17.263Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 review reopened: keep completed SDK adoption and first-round proofs. Fix base publication order so a crash between scalar update and terminal close cannot make sync reverse Azure. Complete the outbox outcome state machine, including definitive rejections and corrected-plan retries. Add semantic SIGKILL convergence assertions using the next sync, deterministic randomized fake-Azure model coverage, both fixed cases and function-only revert proofs. Targeted/typecheck/docstring checks locally; unchanged npm/Bun CI release gates. No merge, mentions or thread replies."
  "2026-10-26T03:48:22.873Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 implementation: terminal sync now commits scalars without ado_sync_base/ado_rev, then a matched status-only close, then agreement/revision publication last against the close revision. Non-terminal fields and their base stay in one conditional SDK update. All relation operations finish before publication. The fixed SIGKILL case restarts with ordinary sync and preserves Closed on both sides; every reopening PATCH is forbidden. Native SDK close clears assignment, so the settled crash oracle includes that existing lifecycle policy rather than incorrectly requiring zero PATCHes."
  "2026-10-26T03:48:24.904Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 outbox: one total state/event table and executor now own prepared, dispatched, observed and rejected. Typed AdoHttpError preserves response status; definitive 4xx except 408 and revision refusals become rejected. Only durable rejection permits corrected type/fields/projection/key to replace a create plan. 5xx, 408, invalid JSON and connection/timeout failures retain unknown dispatch and resolve original markers/history before retry. Successful lookup/historical proof is durably observed; a proven foreign PATCH revision becomes rejected. Unknown creation still cannot blindly resend."
  "2026-10-26T03:48:26.781Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 targeted command passed 17/17 tests: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2|conditional outbox PATCH replay|pending PATCH bases|blocking review|successive mapped edits\" test/sync.test.ts . Seeded model: 36 create sequences, 53 definitive rejections corrected, 16 ambiguous outcomes held until provider visibility, 36 unique observed identities; 33 PATCH sequences, 14 definitive refusals retried, exactly 33 accepted revisions/unique links/history effects. Three real SIGKILL rejection boundaries distinguish durable rejection from lost proof. Typecheck/build/test-typecheck and 98 documented declarations pass; whitespace check clean. Complete semantic crash matrix and source coverage are running."
  "2026-10-26T03:55:24.579Z",codex-agent,"Additional total-state correction: a never-dispatched prepared plan may safely refresh to current inputs after looking up its old marker. Retaining stale prepared fields could otherwise overwrite a mapped local edit after an interruption before dispatch. The new real-tracker regression changes title, body and Azure type before retry and proves one creation with the latest input. Unknown dispatched and observed plans remain immutable. Semantic crash matrix passed 196 fault cells across six scenarios, including terminal import and terminal export, using next ordinary sync and assertions against every reopening PATCH."
  "2026-10-26T03:56:54.111Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 revert proof, base ordering: restored only the local update grouping function from e677059 and rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2 fixed case: SIGKILL\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1: next ordinary sync reopened Azure to New instead of preserving Closed. Restored the function and rebuilt. Agreement/revision publication now follows the durable close, with every commit matched to the preceding revision."
  "2026-10-26T03:56:56.596Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 revert proof, outcome classification: reverted only SyncOutbox.execute to dispatch, call and success recording without the failure transition. Rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2 fixed case: definitive\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 because corrected export remained ADO_CONFLICT after HTTP 400. Restored and rebuilt. Definitive rejection is now durably recorded; ambiguous failures retain the original dispatch key."
  "2026-10-26T03:56:58.245Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 revert proof, corrected plans: disabled only the safe replan branch inside SyncOutbox.create and rebuilt. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"round-2 fixed case: definitive\" test/sync.test.ts failed 1/1 because the rejected plan could not accept corrected input. Restored and rebuilt. Latest focused command passes 18/18, including changed inputs before any dispatch, both fixed cases, 69 seeded sequences, PATCH replay, and three real rejection-response/journal crash boundaries. Pinned pm linked run previously passed 17/17 before the added prepared-input case; the new restored command includes it. No SDK version or thresholds changed."
  "2026-10-26T03:58:12.267Z",codex-agent,"Final round-2 source diagnostic: both sync.ts and sync-outbox.ts reach 100% lines, branches and functions with the full non-matrix regression selection; the separate six-scenario semantic matrix passed 196 fault cells. Final differential against recorded origin baseline 7f44a1d passes 14/14 comparisons across 140 public items. Typecheck, test typecheck, 98 documented declarations, changelog and whitespace checks pass. CI remains the full four-dimension npm/Bun release-gate evidence. Preparing one repair commit with PM records, then incorporating the newer main release-policy commit before CI; no SDK dependency change."
  "2026-10-26T04:14:42.734Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 complete repair CI PASS on merged head 9fe7628 (repair 4c29583 plus current main): https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40266894633 . All 4 jobs succeeded: Node 22, Node 26, npm release gate and Bun release gate. Each job ran 469/469 tests in both V8 and independent statement passes, zero failures/skips. All four coverage dimensions 100% across 9 required sources; statements 1607/1607. CodeQL passed: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/actions/runs/40266894638 . Unchanged thresholds and SDK pin. Final pinned pm linked run passes 18/18; local non-matrix diagnostic 83/83 with both sync modules at 100% lines/branches/functions. Typecheck, test typecheck, 98 documented declarations, changelog, strict health, privacy, whitespace and history-prefix checks pass. No standalone lint script exists."
  "2026-10-26T04:14:44.022Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 final evidence: base and acknowledged revision publish LAST after guarded native close; non-terminal values/base stay one conditional commit. Six scenarios cover 98 observed boundaries and 196 edit/SIGKILL cells, restarting with ordinary sync and rejecting transient reopening PATCHes. Three additional real rejection crash boundaries distinguish durable rejected state from lost proof. Seeded model: 36 create sequences (53 definitive rejections corrected, 16 unknown outcomes held until provider proof, 36 unique observed identities) and 33 PATCH sequences (14 refusals retried; 33 unique accepted revisions/links/history effects). Three function-only behavioral reverts each fail 1/1; restored focused command passes 18/18. Differential remains 14/14 comparisons across 140 public tracker items. Unknown creates, including rejection responses lost before journaling or older dispatched records without proof, still require provider visibility/uniqueness or an explicit recovery contract; no blind resend is allowed or approved. Releasing adoption claim for orchestrator verification; both PM items remain unclosed."
  "2026-10-26T23:34:27.666Z",codex-agent,"Re-review reopened for the three-way merge BASE class. Replace whole accepted-remote recovery promotion with per-key effect provenance; only post-operation local/Azure read-back agreement may advance stored base or acknowledged revision. Consolidate all base/revision writes, including resolution, behind one function. Add the reproduced scalar-PATCH/remote-link interruption plus a >=500-sequence two-writer reference model, retain earlier fixed cases, perform model revert proof, and run targeted/typecheck/docstring checks plus unchanged npm/Bun CI gates. Local tests use at most two workers; no concurrent full suites. No merge, mentions or thread replies."
  "2026-10-26T23:47:53.846Z",codex-agent,"R3 implementation progress: recovery now carries owned scalar-effect provenance instead of promoting the accepted remote snapshot into a base. A new advanceSyncBase function reads the actual SDK tracker and expanded Azure object after operations, advances only equal keys, and acknowledges a revision only on full agreement. Actual local relation projection is independent of remote snapshots. Sync and resolution base/revision publication both delegate to this function; early link/create acknowledgments were removed. Remaining unequal keys yield typed conflict. Partial initial bases explicitly mark unknown keys. Native close runs through the SDK, followed by an explicit SDK assignment update when needed so successful import has equal mapped values. Installed SDK declarations and upstream open issues were searched: commitWorkspaceTransaction exists; BulkItemCloseMutation still has no match signature. No acceptance is being deferred as an SDK gap. Focused cases compile; model/review regression and full validation are next."
  "2026-10-27T00:11:10.386Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 fixed case now retains a remote relation across interruption immediately after scalar PATCH. Sync and resolution publish only through advanceSyncBase using actual local graph and expanded Azure read-back; recovery proof is limited to scalar keys actually sent and never substitutes an accepted snapshot for common base. Added a deterministic 512-sequence two-sided model with native SDK trackers, recording Azure server, interruption/resume and further edits; validating its independent edit ledger now. Existing SDK pin and all coverage thresholds are unchanged."
  "2026-10-27T00:18:14.250Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 differential passes 14/14 comparisons over 140 public items in two non-git read-only snapshot corpora, with writable copies for import. Receipts, values and net history patches match the original main build. Intentional history differences are guarded SDK transaction messages, patch path ordering and a separate final agreement event (two events instead of one). Strict isolated-identity health passes; only the existing advisory telemetry queue is reported and no telemetry configuration was touched. Typecheck and 111/111 documented declarations pass. The 512-sequence model caught a test misuse of strict SDK dependency removal (selectors for absent edges), now corrected to remove only existing rows."
  "2026-10-27T00:27:09.791Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 behavioural revert proof: revert ONLY mergeSyncValues so owned recovery assigns base = effect.accepted (the whole accepted Azure snapshot). Command: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"round-3 model\" test/sync.test.ts. Result: 0/1 pass, 1/1 fail in the reference model reviewed-case prefix: expected the remote relation count 1, observed 0 (recovery erased an unimported remote edit). Restored the function immediately; dedicated fixed case passes. No SDK or test fixture was replaced for the revert. The full 512-sequence run and complete gates remain in progress."
  "2026-10-27T00:37:33.905Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 restored targeted checks pass 13/13. advanceSyncBase and readBaseRevisions have 100% V8 lines, branches and functions in that focused run. Added per-key witnessed Azure revisions inside the base so acknowledged scalar proof is retired independently when unrelated relations still prevent a whole-item revision acknowledgement. A dedicated reference test requires a typed conflict for later competing scalar edits despite an older owned effect. recoverEffects now names its returned original/accepted request evidence explicitly; it never returns or publishes common base. Added real SIGKILL matrices for simultaneous local scalar/remote relation edits and pending-PATCH recovery, covering all observed REST/local/outbox boundaries. New matrices and the 512-sequence run are in progress."
  "2026-10-27T00:45:23.221Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 real-process acceptance passes 62/62 tests: 60 edit/SIGKILL fault cells plus two scenario parents, over 30 observed boundaries in simultaneous scalar/link sync and pending PATCH recovery. Both new matrices check settled intended values, preserved annotations, unique remote and local identities and replay with no additional creation. Final differential passes 14/14 across 140 public items with only documented history grouping, transaction markers, path ordering and internal per-key revision coordinates differing. Pinned pm test --run --progress linked selections pass 5/5 fixed cases and 4/4 agreement contracts. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstrings and changelog pass. The inherited 500-sequence normalization model passed 500 sequences, 500 exact replays and 50 stale replays; the new two-sided 512-sequence model and package-wide local regression selection are still running. CI npm/Bun release gates will provide complete exact-head coverage evidence."
  "2026-10-27T01:16:52.561Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 local model completed: seed 0x37a9c521, 512 sequences, 230 interrupted commands, 444 converged retries and 68 typed conflicts. All scalar/relationship actor categories were exercised on both sides; successful syncs matched actual stores and every published base key had an equality witness. This is the first local model receipt; full CI reruns the complete model on its exact checkout. Final-head function-only proofs each fail 1/1: promoting the accepted snapshot deletes the remote link (0 instead of 1), and removing per-key proof retirement chooses remote instead of reporting a competing scalar conflict. Restored agreement contracts pass 4/4. Added two caller regressions, both passing: native SDK validation leaves item/base untouched; scalar resolution publishes only matching scalar keys, leaves an unimported link out of base and allows ordinary sync plus replay without another PATCH. Broad local selection passes 288/289; only packed-install setup fails because npm registry metadata fetch times out, reproduced in isolation. Curl can reach the public registry; no host network configuration changed. CI run 40428452207 is running the full npm/Bun release gates and Node matrix."
